  "review": [
    "Only the UI control bounds and drag capture lifetime change. The shared controls contain no PCM rendering, gain, chip engine, scheduling transport or WASM changes.",
    "The measured Playground caller retains its original fixed min/max bounds and never calls updateRange or cancelDrag. Static-range pointer movement computes the same interval as before.",
    "The sole new DOM event is lostpointercapture cleanup, which removes a CSS drag marker without sending a parameter edit. Range updates are passive and cancel stale capture before changing local bounds.",
    "The complete current body reconstructs the exact independently authenticated receipt01 after-body, then receipt01 reconstructs the original measured body. All four measured reports and receipt01 remain byte-for-byte unchanged. Future edits, imports and cache queries are not covered."
  ]
